{"content":[{"c":["GAD*, Valley of"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Translation of a Hebrew phrase in ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.24.5","r":"2Sam.24.5","rawR":"2Sam.24.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.24.5","value":"2Sam.24.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Samuel 24:5"},", meaning literally “the river or streambed of Gad.” It is rendered “in the midst of the river of Gad” (",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"), “in the middle of the valley, toward Gad” (",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"), “the valley of Gad” (",{"c":["asv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},") and “in the direction of Gad” (",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). The valley of Gad was the beginning point for David’s census, and the “river” or “valley” is undoubtedly the Arnon."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"GadValleyof","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Samuel 24:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.24.5","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.24.5","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.24.5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2112386aff2fafb9160a10fd15a0f540fb302547154234bc5b4e92833313295f","sourceItemName":"GadValleyof","sourceItemOrder":13,"sourceMember":"Articles/G.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"GadValleyof","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Gad*, Valley of","title":"Gad*, Valley of","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}